# -w and -std=c++17 are Clang/GCC-style flags; we scope them to the Unix hosts via
# --enable_platform_specific_config (which auto-applies build:linux / build:macos /
# build:windows by host OS) instead of passing them globally, because both misbehave
# under cl.exe:
#   -w: warnings vary across Clang/GCC/MSVC and the version disparity can turn some
#   into errors, so we silence them on Unix. Under cl.exe -w becomes /w, but abseil
#   adds /W3 as a per-target copt (ABSL_MSVC_FLAGS) that Bazel places after our global
#   copt, so /W3 wins -- defeating the suppression and emitting a D9025 ("overriding
#   '/w' with '/W3'") on abseil units. Leaving Windows unflagged removes the /w, so
#   there is no conflict and no D9025; the residual C-warnings (e.g. C4715 in
#   protobuf's Objective-C codegen host tool) are cosmetic and the build succeeds. A
#   global Windows /W0 would not help -- it just re-triggers D9025 against abseil's /W3.
#   -std=c++17: cl.exe ignores the gcc-style spelling (emitting D9002) and needs
#   /std:c++17, which the Windows build passes explicitly (see native-prebuilds.yml);
#   keeping -std=c++17 off the Windows command line drops that per-unit D9002 noise
#   without changing the standard actually compiled against.
common --enable_platform_specific_config
build --experimental_isolated_extension_usages
build:linux --cxxopt="-std=c++17" --copt="-w"
build:macos --cxxopt="-std=c++17" --copt="-w"

build:wasm --incompatible_enable_cc_toolchain_resolution
build:wasm --platforms=@emsdk//:platform_wasm

# Native N-API addon (private_set_intersection/napi). Enables the threaded
# per-element EC paths in parallel_ec.cpp / psi_server.cpp / psi_client.cpp.
# The WASM build never uses this config, so it stays single-threaded and
# byte-identical. This config alone builds a host-native addon for local checks:
#   bazel build -c opt --config=napi //private_set_intersection/napi:addon
# The SHIPPED per-platform prebuilds add the hermetic zig cross-toolchain and,
# on Linux, --force_pic -- which makes the object a proper shared library with a
# dlopen-safe (dynamic) TLS model. A local build without --force_pic runs on the
# host but is not what ships; see .github/workflows/native-prebuilds.yml for the
# exact per-leg command.
build:napi --copt=-DPSI_ENABLE_THREADS
